T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the mathematical model of a series RLC resonant circuit and solve for its transient step response using `scipy.integrate.solve_ivp`.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Series RLC Circuit Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Applying Kirchhoff's Voltage Law \(KVL\) around a series RLC loop excited by step voltage) Tj
T*
(   $V_{in}\(t\)$:) Tj
T*
(   $$L \\frac{di\(t\)}{dt} + R i\(t\) + v_C\(t\) = V_{in}\(t\)$$) Tj
T*
(   Since the current through the capacitor is $i\(t\) = C \\frac{dv_C\(t\)}{dt}$, we substitute to) Tj
T*
(   obtain the second-order ordinary differential equation:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\frac{d^2 v_C\(t\)}{dt^2} + \\frac{R}{L} \\frac{dv_C\(t\)}{dt} + \\frac{1}{L C} v_C\(t\) = \\frac{1}{L) Tj
T*
(   C} V_{in}\(t\)$$) Tj
T*
(   Damping ratio $\\zeta = \\frac{R}{2} \\sqrt{\\frac{C}{L}}$ and undamped natural frequency $\\omega_0) Tj
T*
(   = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{L C}}$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   State-Space First-Order System Transformation:) Tj
T*
(   Let state variables be $x_1 = v_C$ and $x_2 = \\frac{dv_C}{dt} = \\frac{i}{C}$:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\begin{bmatrix} \\dot{x}_1 \\\\ \\dot{x}_2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{LC}) Tj
T*
(   & -\\frac{R}{L} \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} x_1 \\\\ x_2 \\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\) Tj
T*
(   \\frac{V_{in}}{LC} \\end{bmatrix}$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   SciPy Implementation:) Tj
