(   [Problem Statement]: Compare causal IIR filtering \(`lfilter`\) versus zero-phase non-causal forward-backward filtering \(`filtfilt`\) with mathematical derivations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Phase Distortion Analysis:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Causal Filtering \(`lfilter`\):) Tj
T*
(   When an input signal $x[n]$ is passed through an IIR filter $H\(z\)$:) Tj
T*
(   $$y_{causal}[n] = \\sum_{k=0}^M b_k x[n-k] - \\sum_{k=1}^N a_k y_{causal}[n-k]$$) Tj
T*
(   Because IIR filters possess non-linear phase responses $\\theta\(\\omega\)$, different frequency) Tj
T*
(   components experience different group delays $\\tau_g\(\\omega\) =) Tj
T*
(   -\\frac{d\\theta\(\\omega\)}{d\\omega}$, distorting pulse waveforms, ECG complexes, and digital radar) Tj
T*
(   echoes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Zero-Phase Forward-Backward Filtering \(`filtfilt`\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Forward filter $x[n]$ through $H\(z\)$ to produce intermediate output $v[n]$.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Time-reverse $v[n]$ to obtain $v[-n]$ and filter through $H\(z\)$ again.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Time-reverse the result to yield final output $y[n]$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Effective System Transfer Function:) Tj
T*
(   $$H_{eff}\(e^{j\\omega}\) = H\(e^{j\\omega}\) \\cdot H^*\(e^{j\\omega}\) = |H\(e^{j\\omega}\)|^2$$) Tj
T*
(   Because $|H\(e^{j\\omega}\)|^2$ is purely real and positive, the overall phase response is) Tj
T*
(   IDENTICALLY ZERO $\\theta_{eff}\(\\omega\) \\equiv 0$. Group delay is exactly zero, completely) Tj
T*
(   preserving signal peak alignments in post-processing applications.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
