(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate and implement the classical 4th-Order Runge-Kutta \(RK4\) numerical ODE solver from scratch in Python.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mathematical Derivation of Classical RK4:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   To solve the initial value problem $\\frac{dy}{dt} = f\(t, y\)$ with $y\(t_0\) = y_0$ and step size) Tj
T*
(   $h$:) Tj
T*
(   $$y_{n+1} = y_n + \\frac{h}{6} \(k_1 + 2 k_2 + 2 k_3 + k_4\)$$) Tj
T*
(   where the four trial slopes are evaluated as:) Tj
T*
(   - $k_1 = f\(t_n, y_n\)$) Tj
T*
(   - $k_2 = f\\left\( t_n + \\frac{h}{2}, y_n + \\frac{h}{2} k_1 \\right\)$) Tj
T*
(   - $k_3 = f\\left\( t_n + \\frac{h}{2}, y_n + \\frac{h}{2} k_2 \\right\)$) Tj
T*
(   - $k_4 = f\(t_n + h, y_n + h k_3\)$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Global Truncation Error: $\\mathcal{O}\(h^4\)$, delivering fourth-order polynomial accuracy with) Tj
T*
(   exceptional stability margins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   def rk4_integrator\(f, t0, y0, t_end, h\):) Tj
T*
(   t_values = [t0]) Tj
T*
(   y_values = [y0]) Tj
T*
(   t, y = t0, y0) Tj
T*
(   while t < t_end:) Tj
T*
(   k1 = f\(t, y\)) Tj
T*
(   k2 = f\(t + 0.5 * h, y + 0.5 * h * k1\)) Tj
T*
(   k3 = f\(t + 0.5 * h, y + 0.5 * h * k2\)) Tj
T*
(   k4 = f\(t + h, y + h * k3\)) Tj
T*
(   y = y + \(h / 6.0\) * \(k1 + 2*k2 + 2*k3 + k4\)) Tj
T*
(   t += h) Tj
T*
(   t_values.append\(t\)) Tj
T*
(   y_values.append\(y\)) Tj
T*
(   return np.array\(t_values\), np.array\(y_values\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
