(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate high-precision pitch and dominant frequency detection in audio signals using FFT with parabolic interpolation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   FFT Peak Detection with Parabolic Interpolation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Due to discrete FFT bin spacing $\\Delta f = f_s / N$, the true continuous peak frequency often) Tj
T*
(   lies between two discrete bins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def estimate_exact_pitch\(signal_frame, fs\):) Tj
T*
(   N = len\(signal_frame\)) Tj
T*
(   # Apply Hanning window) Tj
T*
(   windowed = signal_frame * np.hanning\(N\)) Tj
T*
(   spectrum = np.abs\(np.fft.rfft\(windowed\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Find maximum discrete bin) Tj
T*
(   k = np.argmax\(spectrum\)) Tj
T*
(   if k == 0 or k == len\(spectrum\) - 1:) Tj
T*
(   return k * \(fs / N\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Parabolic interpolation on log-magnitude) Tj
T*
(   alpha = np.log\(spectrum[k - 1]\)) Tj
T*
(   beta = np.log\(spectrum[k]\)) Tj
T*
(   gamma = np.log\(spectrum[k + 1]\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Fractional bin offset delta in range [-0.5, 0.5]) Tj
T*
(   delta = 0.5 * \(alpha - gamma\) / \(alpha - 2 * beta + gamma\)) Tj
T*
(   true_freq = \(k + delta\) * \(fs / N\)) Tj
T*
(   return true_freq) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
