(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate diode I-V Shockley equation parameter extraction using non-linear least squares curve fitting with `scipy.optimize.curve_fit`.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Diode Characteristic Parameter Extraction:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Shockley ideal diode equation relates diode current $I_D$ to applied forward voltage $V_D$:) Tj
T*
(   $$I_D\(V_D\) = I_s \\left\( e^{\\frac{q V_D}{\\eta k_B T}} - 1 \\right\)$$) Tj
T*
(   Let thermal voltage $V_T = \\frac{k_B T}{q} \\approx 0.0259$ V at 300 K.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
(   from scipy.optimize import curve_fit) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   VT = 0.0259 # 25.9 mV thermal voltage) Tj
T*
(   def shockley_diode\(V, Is, eta\):) Tj
T*
(   return Is * \(np.exp\(V / \(eta * VT\)\) - 1.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Experimental forward voltage and current data) Tj
T*
(   V_meas = np.array\([0.45, 0.50, 0.55, 0.60, 0.65, 0.70]\)) Tj
T*
(   I_meas = np.array\([1.2e-5, 8.5e-5, 5.8e-4, 3.9e-3, 2.6e-2, 1.7e-1]\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Non-linear least squares fit with bounds) Tj
T*
(   popt, pcov = curve_fit\(shockley_diode, V_meas, I_meas, p0=[1e-12, 1.5], bounds=\(1e-15, [1e-6,) Tj
T*
(   3.0]\)\)) Tj
T*
(   Is_fit, eta_fit = popt) Tj
T*
(   print\(f'Extracted Is = {Is_fit:.3e} A, Ideality Factor eta = {eta_fit:.2f}'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
