(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture of a Software-Defined Radio \(SDR\) Costas Loop for carrier phase synchronization in BPSK.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Costas Loop Architecture for Suppressed Carrier Tracking:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   In BPSK, direct phase-locked loops fail because the carrier is suppressed by random $\\pm 1$) Tj
T*
(   symbol transitions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Costas Loop Components:) Tj
T*
(   1. In-phase \(I\) and Quadrature \(Q\) Mixers: Demodulate the received signal with local NCO) Tj
T*
(   orthogonal references $\\cos\(\\omega_c t + \\hat{\\theta}\)$ and $-\\sin\(\\omega_c t + \\hat{\\theta}\)$.) Tj
T*
(   2. Arm Low-Pass Filters: Eliminate high-frequency $2\\omega_c$ sum components, leaving baseband) Tj
T*
(   $I\(t\) \\approx A d\(t\) \\cos\(\\theta_e\)$ and $Q\(t\) \\approx A d\(t\) \\sin\(\\theta_e\)$ where $\\theta_e =) Tj
T*
(   \\theta - \\hat{\\theta}$.) Tj
T*
(   3. Phase Error Detector: Multiplies the two arms: $e\(t\) = I\(t\) \\cdot Q\(t\) \\approx \\frac{1}{2}) Tj
T*
(   A^2 d^2\(t\) \\sin\(2\\theta_e\) = \\frac{1}{2} A^2 \\sin\(2\\theta_e\)$.) Tj
T*
(   Because $d^2\(t\) = \(\\pm 1\)^2 = +1$, data modulation is completely stripped away! The error) Tj
T*
(   signal drives a loop filter that steers the NCO frequency to achieve lock.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
