(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate continuous-time state-space simulation of a closed-loop PID DC motor angular speed controller.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   DC Motor Dynamic Model:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Electromechanical state equations:) Tj
T*
(   $$L \\frac{di}{dt} + R i = V - K_e \\omega, \\quad J \\frac{d\\omega}{dt} + b \\omega = K_t i - T_L$$) Tj
T*
(   PID Control Law: $V\(t\) = K_p e\(t\) + K_i \\int e\(t\) dt + K_d \\frac{de\(t\)}{dt}$ where error $e\(t\)) Tj
T*
(   = \\omega_{target} - \\omega\(t\)$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
(   from scipy.integrate import solve_ivp) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   R, L, Kt, Ke, J, b = 2.0, 0.5, 0.1, 0.1, 0.02, 0.01) Tj
T*
(   Kp, Ki, Kd = 15.0, 2.0, 0.5) Tj
T*
(   w_target = 100.0 # 100 rad/s) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def motor_system\(t, state\):) Tj
T*
(   i, w, e_integral = state) Tj
T*
(   e = w_target - w) Tj
T*
(   V_control = np.clip\(Kp * e + Ki * e_integral, 0.0, 24.0\) # Saturated 24V supply) Tj
T*
(   di = \(V_control - R * i - Ke * w\) / L) Tj
T*
(   dw = \(Kt * i - b * w\) / J) Tj
T*
(   return [di, dw, e]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   sol = solve_ivp\(motor_system, \(0, 2.0\), [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], t_eval=np.linspace\(0, 2.0, 500\)\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
