(   [Problem Statement]: Implement an adaptive Wiener filter in Python for optimal signal restoration in colored noise environments.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Wiener Deconvolution Formulation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Wiener filtering minimizes mean-square estimation error between desired clean signal $s\(t\)$ and) Tj
T*
(   noisy measurement $x\(t\) = \(s * h\)\(t\) + n\(t\)$:) Tj
T*
(   $$G\(f\) = \\frac{H^*\(f\) S_{ss}\(f\)}{|H\(f\)|^2 S_{ss}\(f\) + S_{nn}\(f\)}$$) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def wiener_restore\(x, h_impulse, snr_linear\):) Tj
T*
(   N = len\(x\)) Tj
T*
(   H = np.fft.rfft\(h_impulse, n=N\)) Tj
T*
(   X = np.fft.rfft\(x, n=N\)) Tj
T*
(   # Frequency-domain Wiener transfer function) Tj
T*
(   G = np.conj\(H\) / \(np.abs\(H\)**2 + 1.0 / snr_linear\)) Tj
T*
(   s_est = np.fft.irfft\(X * G, n=N\)) Tj
T*
(   return s_est) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
