(   [Problem Statement]: Design an FIR Hilbert Transformer filter in Python for creating single-sideband \(SSB\) modulated communications signals.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Hilbert Transformer Filter Design:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   An ideal Hilbert transformer introduces a constant $90^\\circ$ phase shift \($-j$ for $\\omega >) Tj
T*
(   0$ and $+j$ for $\\omega < 0$\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   from scipy import signal) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def create_ssb_modulator\(message, fc, fs\):) Tj
T*
(   t = np.arange\(len\(message\)\) / fs) Tj
T*
(   # Design 65-tap Type III Hilbert FIR filter) Tj
T*
(   h_fir = signal.firwin\(65, [0.05, 0.95], pass_zero=False, fs=fs\)) Tj
T*
(   m_hilbert = signal.lfilter\(h_fir, 1.0, message\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Compensate FIR group delay \(65 - 1\)/2 = 32 samples) Tj
T*
(   m_delayed = np.roll\(message, -32\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Lower Single-Sideband \(LSSB\): m\(t\) cos\(w_c t\) + m_hat\(t\) sin\(w_c t\)) Tj
T*
(   carrier_cos = np.cos\(2 * np.pi * fc * t\)) Tj
T*
(   carrier_sin = np.sin\(2 * np.pi * fc * t\)) Tj
T*
(   s_lssb = m_delayed * carrier_cos + m_hilbert * carrier_sin) Tj
T*
(   return s_lssb) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
